 # bench-locale-pack (benchmark fixture)
 
-A 19-language override layer for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), written in the
-0.1.1-era style: it patches the locale runtime's lookup chain so a selected
-third language wins over DSH's native zh/en while DSH's active locale stays
-on `en`, ships a custom switcher row into the settings General section, and
-persists the selection in localStorage (`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`).
-Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub. The host is moving to
-dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A 19-language pack for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), migrated to the native
+language API of dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2: each curated language registers through
+`ctx.locale.addLanguage({ id, label, fallback })`, every (namespace, language)
+dictionary registers through `ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)`, and the
+added languages appear in DSH's own language row in the settings General
+section (the `settings.general.item` slot that `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale`
+registers). The selection is persisted by the locale service as
+`locale.preference` in the Host settings document (`$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml`
+on loopback pages) — the pack mutates no locale runtime and keeps no storage
+of its own. Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub.
+`cordis.patch.yml` inserts the bundle row. The host is on dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+
+## Migrated entry points (0.1.1-era → 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+The 0.1.1-era surface entered third languages by monkey-patching the locale
+runtime's lookup chain, shipped its own switcher row into the settings General
+section, persisted the selection in localStorage
+(`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`), and provided a `betterLocale` service for
+third-party dictionary registration. The harness now ships the same entry
+points, so those layers are retired:
+
+| Retired entry point | Native coverage |
+| --- | --- |
+| `LocaleRuntime.prototype.lookup` patch | `ctx.locale.addLanguage` + `ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)` feed the native fallback-chain lookup |
+| Custom row in `settings.general.item` | `dsh-client-locale` registers its own `language` row in that slot and lists every added language |
+| `dsh-plugin-better-locale:active` in localStorage | `ctx.locale.setLocale` writes `locale.preference` through the Host settings service |
+| `betterLocale` service | third-party packs inject the official `locale` service |
+
+The pack still owns the language data itself: the 19 curated languages and
+their dictionaries (the fixture keeps 3 languages × 2 keys — the real dicts
+carry ~893 keys per language).
+
+Scope of the native surface (host-owned, not pack behavior):
+
+- `locale.preference` is durable only on loopback pages. On a non-loopback
+  page the Client withholds the settings scope, so the selection stays
+  process-local for that browser session — the retired localStorage layer
+  survived that case; the native surface deliberately does not.
+- `ctx.locale.addLanguage` throws on a duplicate id, so a curated id that DSH
+  later ships as a built-in would fail this pack's `apply` (built-ins are
+  `zh`/`en` at 0.1.2-alpha.2).
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
